The Google rating is the simplest trick in this post: stop reading the car park's page and open the review tab.

Two things matter, and the second matters more. The rating shows the average, and the volume shows how much that average means. A lot with 5.0 and 10 reviews says nothing. A lot with 4.1 and 274 reviews says a good deal more, because the sample crossed months, holidays and night shifts.

Then filter by most recent and read the three worst from the last week. That is where what nobody writes about leaving the car at Afonso Pena Airport shows up. You are not looking for praise, you are looking for a pattern: if the same problem appears in five different accounts, it belongs to the lot, not to the customer.

