## Frequently asked questions

### Does a car park in Curitiba answer for theft of the car?

Yes. The STJ's Precedent 130 says a company answers to its customer for damage to or theft of a vehicle occurring in its car park. The liability is strict: it is enough to prove use of the service and the damage. That is why the entry receipt, with plate and time, is the most important document of the trip.

### Do the Afonso Pena partners have cameras and a 24-hour gate?

Both declare 24h cameras, a controlled gate and 24-hour staffing on their record, on 17 September 2026, plus an insured car park and a 5-minute transfer. These are the branch's declarations, and Movepark audits neither a camera nor a third party's policy.

### Do I need to record a scratch before leaving the lot in Curitiba?

Yes, and it is the rule that decides the case for anyone leaving the car at Afonso Pena Airport. With the vehicle still inside, the damage is within the safekeeping period. After the exit, it becomes an argument about where it happened. Stop, photograph it with the lot in the background, call the team and ask for a written, signed record before starting the engine.

### In Curitiba does the key stay with me or with the lot?

With you. It is safe to leave the car at Afonso Pena Airport without handing over the key: both partners declare self-park, so you park it yourself, and neither runs a valet. That reduces the number of people with access to the inside of the car, and leaves the entry check in your hands.

### Will the battery go flat if I leave the car 30 days in Curitiba?

It can. An alarm, an infotainment system and a keyless fob draw current even when parked, and above 20 days a car with a battery more than three years old usually needs help. Both partners at this location declare battery maintenance on their record, which helps on your return.

### Does a covered space protect the car from theft at Afonso Pena Airport?

No. Cover protects against sun, rain and hail, which preserves paintwork, rubber and the dashboard on a long stay, and in Curitiba that weighs because of the frequent rain. On the 27 October 2026 table, it costs R$ 49.00 more over seven days at Abbapark. Protection of property comes from the gate, the camera and the record.

### What is the minimum stay for anyone leaving the car at Afonso Pena Airport?

It is three days at both partners, across every type of space, on 17 September 2026. A trip of one or two nights pays all three days, so on a very short trip it is worth comparing with the official car park, which charges for the period used.

### Can the car park refuse to hand the car over without a receipt?

It can, and it does so for your protection when you leave the car at Afonso Pena Airport. The receipt links the plate to the entry record and stops anyone from collecting the vehicle. If you lost the document, bring photo ID, the vehicle's papers and the booking confirmation. Most lots resolve it with a data check and a signature.$f173$
