## The car parks at Curitiba Airport, side by side

Curitiba/Afonso Pena International Airport, IATA code CWB, is in São José dos Pinhais, in the Curitiba metropolitan region. It has two Movepark partner lots. Both state a 5-minute transfer to the terminal and a three-day minimum. The prices below are from the 27 October 2026 table.

| Lot | Distance from terminal | 7 days, uncovered | 7 days, covered | 7 days, premium |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Abbapark | 2.6 km | R$ 153.30 | R$ 202.30 | R$ 216.30 |
| Nationpark | 1.4 km | R$ 181.30 | R$ 237.30 | R$ 251.30 |

The difference between the two is small and predictable. Nationpark charges R$ 28.00 more for the week in an uncovered spot, and in exchange sits 1.2 km closer to the terminal.

### 1. Abbapark: the lowest figure in every band

It is at R. Norberto de Brito, 574, Centro, in São José dos Pinhais, 2.6 km from the terminal. The stated transfer is 5 minutes, with a 60-minute grace period. It runs three spot types: uncovered, covered and premium. On the 27 October 2026 table, thirty days in an uncovered spot come to R$ 627.00. It also charges less than the other lot in every length-of-stay band.

### 2. Nationpark: the closest to the terminal

It is at Av. Rocha Pombo, 2853, Águas Belas, in São José dos Pinhais, 1.4 km from the terminal. That is a little under half the distance of the other lot. It is also the only one of the two to state how often the van runs: every 15 minutes. At an airport lot that matters, because the wait usually costs more time than the ride. On the 27 October 2026 table, thirty days in an uncovered spot come to R$ 747.00.

### 3. The official Afonso Pena car park

It sits inside the complex, reachable on foot, with 4,032 covered spaces according to the airport itself. In the manual query of 27 August 2026, daily rates started at R$ 43.15 in the multi-storey car park, Area A. In the shaded lots, the floor was R$ 28.63 in Area B and R$ 15.90 in Area C. The rate belongs to the operator and moves with demand. That is why it is the option that makes sense for a stay of a few hours: both partners charge a three-day minimum.

## Which of the Curitiba Airport car parks fits your case?

There is no single best car park at Curitiba Airport for every case. The right one depends on the length of the trip and the spot type. The rule of thumb runs like this:

- **A trip of up to two days:** the official one usually comes out ahead, because it charges for the time used. The partners' three-day minimum means a one-day trip pays the same as a three-day one.
- **Lowest total among the partners, from three days up:** Abbapark. It is the floor of the two lots in every band on the 27 October 2026 table. The official Area C advertised a lower daily rate, from R$ 15.90 in the collection of 27 August 2026, with a rate that moves with demand.
- **Least travel time:** Nationpark, 1.4 km away and with a van every 15 minutes stated on its page.
- **A covered spot:** either partner. Against the official covered spot, the cheapest covered partner spot comes out 35% lower over fifteen days, with the partner on the 27 October 2026 table and the official lot in the collection of 27 August 2026.

## What to check before choosing in Curitiba

- **The three-day minimum:** it applies at both partners. A one-day trip pays the same as a three-day one.
- **Spot type:** uncovered is the floor. Between Abbapark's uncovered and premium spots there is R$ 63.00 of difference over the week on the 27 October 2026 table.
- **Distance:** 1.4 km against 2.6 km, with the same stated five-minute transfer at both lots.
- **Online rate against counter rate:** the gap is around 10% for uncovered spots on the 27 October 2026 table, and zero for covered ones.

The full table by length of stay is in [the price of parking at Afonso Pena Airport](/blog/preco-estacionamento-aeroporto-afonso-pena-curitiba-saiba-tudo-aqui/). The metre-by-metre comparison is in [the closest car park to Afonso Pena Airport](/blog/conheca-o-estacionamento-mais-proximo-do-aeroporto-afonso-pena-em-2024/). And the route to the lowest total, lever by lever, is in [cheap parking at Curitiba Airport](/blog/estacionamento-barato-aeroporto-curitiba/).

## How this comparison was gathered

Distance and transfer time come from each unit's page in the Movepark system. Distance is calculated in the database, as a straight line to the terminal. The partner prices are those of the 27 October 2026 table, read from the booking engine, the same ones that close a booking. Each partner can adjust its own table at any time. The official rate does not pass through the engine. It was collected by hand from the operator's page, on 27 August 2026, and is a "from" figure that moves with demand. The live price is on the [Afonso Pena Airport page](/en/airport-parking/curitiba-airport). Airport traffic figures are on the [ANAC statistics portal](https://www.anac.gov.br/assuntos/dados-e-estatisticas).

## Frequently asked questions

### How many partner car parks are there at Afonso Pena today?

Two in August 2026: Nationpark, 1.4 km from the terminal with a van every 15 minutes, and Abbapark, 2.6 km out. Both state a 5-minute transfer, 24-hour operation and a three-day minimum. The third name in the comparison is the official car park, inside the complex.

### Does the official car park belong in the comparison?

It does. It wins comfortably on a stay of a few hours or up to two days, because it charges for the time used. In the query of 27 August 2026 its daily rate started at R$ 15.90 in the cheapest area, below the R$ 20.90 a day of Abbapark's uncovered spot over fifteen days on the 27 October 2026 table, with a rate that moves with demand.

### What spot types exist at Afonso Pena?

Three at both partners: uncovered, covered and premium. On the 27 October 2026 table a week at Abbapark costs R$ 153.30, R$ 202.30 and R$ 216.30 in that order, with the same address and the same transfer for all three.

### What separates the two partner lots in Curitiba?

Price and distance, because the stated service is similar at both. On the 27 October 2026 table Abbapark charges R$ 28.00 less for the uncovered week and sits 1.2 km further from the terminal than Nationpark, with the same five-minute transfer.

### How do you compare the Curitiba options without slipping up?

Compare the total for the period in the same spot type. On the 27 October 2026 table, fifteen days in an uncovered spot cost R$ 313.50 at Abbapark and R$ 373.50 at Nationpark, and that is the comparison that makes sense.

### Does a parking ranking go stale?

The figures do, the criteria do not. A lot's table changes over the year. That is why every figure here carries the date it was queried and the link to the live price. Distance, the day minimum and spot types change little, and they are what holds the comparison up.$f180$
