## How much does Viracopos Aeroparking cost?

Viracopos Aeroparking's table has two lines and one anomaly. The site lists R$ 45.50 for the uncovered space and R$ 40.50 for the covered one as a reference figure. It then applies a lower price for anyone paying online.

| Type of space | Reference figure | Daily with online payment | Reference |
|---|---|---|---|
| Uncovered | R$ 45.50 | R$ 34.70 | lot's website, 22/09/2026 |
| Covered | R$ 40.50 | R$ 29.20 | lot's website, 22/09/2026 |

Note that the inversion appears in both columns. On the reference figure as much as on the online price, the covered space is the cheaper one. It is not a typo or a one-day promotion: it is how the lot prices.

The site also advertises a 10% discount for anyone paying straight through the platform. Confirm at booking whether it applies to the already reduced figure or to the reference one. The page does not make that explicit.

### Why does the covered space cost less than the uncovered one?

The lot does not explain, and any explanation here would be a guess. What can be said with certainty is the practical effect: **there is no reason to choose the uncovered space at Viracopos Aeroparking**.

You would pay R$ 5.50 more a day to leave the car in the sun. Over seven days, that is R$ 38.50 thrown away, and over fifteen, R$ 82.50.

At every other lot in the area the logic is the opposite, and the cover costs R$ 5.00 to R$ 15.00 more a day. So check the covered option before settling, even if your habit is to take the first on the list.

![table with Aeroparking's daily rate in Viracopos](/images/blog/viracopos-aeroparking/viracopos-aeroparking-preco-diaria.webp)

## Is Viracopos Aeroparking the closest to the airport?

It is, the closest among the mapped lots outside the complex. That is **2.48 km to the terminal**, measured as a straight line, against 4.1 km for KM64 and 4.75 km for Yellow Parking.

The lot itself describes the location as five minutes from Viracopos Airport. That short distance has a direct effect on your travel morning. In other words: less time in the van, less exposure to traffic and a smaller margin for error.

